cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Brain-to-Text v6.4: Cross-Fit Conformer CTC Decoding with Wide KenLM Beam Search, Phonetic-Neighbour Expansion and Fluency-Gated LLM Score Fusion"
abstract: >-
  A neural-speech decoding pipeline for the Kaggle brain-to-text-25 competition.
  Two Patch-Conv/BiGRU/Conformer acoustic models are trained with phoneme CTC,
  inter-CTC and CR-CTC losses on a trial-level cross-fit of the validation set,
  decoded with a lexicon-constrained KenLM 4-gram beam search (beam 1200, seven
  LM weights), expanded with single-word phonetic-neighbour substitutions, and
  rescored by exact CTC sequence likelihood ensembling plus a QLoRA-adapted
  Llama-3.1-8B under a fluency-gated log-linear fusion. Pool composition is
  selected by session-grouped cross-validation and all weights are tuned out of
  fold and verified on a fold selected on by nothing. Verification-fold WER 3.38%
  (out-of-fold 3.59%); acoustic phoneme error rate 6.88% / 6.89% per fold.
authors:
  - family-names: Biswas
    given-names: Anik
keywords:
